  "name": "ALLERGY DRUG-CHLORAMPHENICOL",
  "code": "2618",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The <strong data-start=\"64\" data-end=\"101\">Chloramphenicol Drug Allergy Test</strong> is typically done to detect <strong data-start=\"130\" data-end=\"171\">hypersensitivity (allergic) reactions</strong> to <strong data-start=\"175\" data-end=\"194\">chloramphenicol</strong>, an antibiotic used to treat bacterial infections, especially in the eyes and ears.</p>\n<p data-start=\"1260\" data-end=\"1305\"><strong data-start=\"1264\" data-end=\"1305\">Types of Reactions to Chloramphenicol</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1306\" data-end=\"1549\">\n<li data-start=\"1306\" data-end=\"1372\">\n<p data-start=\"1308\" data-end=\"1336\"><strong data-start=\"1308\" data-end=\"1335\">Mild allergic reactions</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1339\" data-end=\"1372\">\n<li data-start=\"1339\" data-end=\"1350\">\n<p data-start=\"1341\" data-end=\"1350\">Skin rash</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1353\" data-end=\"1362\">\n<p data-start=\"1355\" data-end=\"1362\">Itching</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1365\" data-end=\"1372\">\n<p data-start=\"1367\" data-end=\"1372\">Hives</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1374\" data-end=\"1549\">\n<p data-start=\"1376\" data-end=\"1433\"><strong data-start=\"1376\" data-end=\"1403\">Serious adverse effects</strong> (not always allergy-related):</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1436\" data-end=\"1549\">\n<li data-start=\"1436\" data-end=\"1476\">\n<p data-start=\"1438\" data-end=\"1476\"><strong data-start=\"1438\" data-end=\"1457\">Aplastic anemia</strong> (rare but serious)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1479\" data-end=\"1508\">\n<p data-start=\"1481\" data-end=\"1508\"><strong data-start=\"1481\" data-end=\"1508\">Bone marrow suppression</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1511\" data-end=\"1549\">\n<p data-start=\"1513\" data-end=\"1549\"><strong data-start=\"1513\" data-end=\"1535\">Gray baby syndrome</strong> (in neonates)</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Test Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Positive (Reactive)</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates <strong>allergic sensitization</strong> to chloramphenicol. The patient may develop allergic reactions upon exposure. Avoid further use.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Negative (Non-Reactive)</strong></td>\n<td>Suggests <strong>no current sensitization</strong> to chloramphenicol. However, clinical judgment is still required if the patient has a strong history of reaction.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Equivocal/Borderline</strong></td>\n<td>Inconclusive result. May require <strong>repeat testing</strong>, <strong>clinical correlation</strong>, or <strong>alternative testing methods</strong>.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
